From: Duron27 <duron27@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 13:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] Weather: a weather can be forced from the F2 menu

To test what the weather changes (the wet ground in the rain, the dust in storms, the clouds), the experimental
graphics' settings in the F2 menu (a3_testing test weather) can hold the weather: changed to it at once and kept
there, whatever the region would choose, until it is set back to -1.
---
 apps/openmw/mwworld/weather.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/apps/openmw/mwworld/weather.cpp b/apps/openmw/mwworld/weather.cpp
index f12f1fa4d1..f762a99e4c 100644
--- a/apps/openmw/mwworld/weather.cpp
+++ b/apps/openmw/mwworld/weather.cpp
@@ -27,6 +27,8 @@
 #include "esmstore.hpp"
 #include "player.hpp"
 
+#include <alpha3/upstream.hpp>
+
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <cmath>
 #include <limits>
@@ -887,6 +889,14 @@ namespace MWWorld
                 }
             }
 
+            // Alpha3: the weather the F2 menu asks for, to test with (a3_testing test weather), at once and kept
+            if (const int forced = Alpha3::forcedWeather(); forced >= 0 && forced <= 9)
+            {
+                const ESM::RefId weather = ESM::Weather::indexToRefId(forced);
+                if (mCurrentWeather != weather || inTransition())
+                    forceWeather(weather);
+            }
+
             updateWeatherTransitions(duration);
         }
 
